-- Total maps from each renderer's prepared op union to the
-- `BackendHelperKind` it renders.
--
-- This is the same enumeration `backend_helper_catalog.brp` already did to
-- build its (now 383) rows, expressed the other direction: given an op value (not
-- yet dispatched to C), which catalog row describes it. It is pure data --
-- no C is rendered here and no emission-context threading is involved. A
-- later prepare-side "helper selection" pass is expected to call these
-- functions per Core node and publish the result before emission, which is
-- what actually lets `--explain-allocations` predict rendered-helper counts
-- from data published before emission (see the commit that added this file
-- for why a printer-side accumulator threaded through `emit.brp` is the
-- wrong shape for that: `emit.brp`'s `emit_*` functions are pure and return
-- plain `String`/`Option[String]`/`FunctionBodyC` with no context-out
-- channel, so bubbling a kind back up would mean rewriting most of that
-- file's return types).
--
-- Each function is a total match over its renderer's op union, matching the
-- exhaustiveness the renderer's own dispatcher already requires; an
-- unhandled op variant fails the build here too. Where an op variant carries
-- a secondary flag that the catalog split into more than one row (see
-- backend_helper_catalog.brp's docstring), this matches on the flag as well.
import:
	../stage_09_core/backend_helper_catalog:
		BackendHelperKind(
			BackendChannelIterHeader,
			BackendChannelIterLoopOpen,
			BackendChannelIterReleaseObject,
			BackendChannelIterSourceBinding,
			BackendChannelIterValueInit,
			BackendChannelRecvTimeoutAttempt,
